{"kind":"request","text":"Hugh: state and ratify a scoped outbound charter, because it is the last thing blocking the connector dogfood and only an operator can do it.\n\nEverything else is now in place. The connector's outbound half is built and reviewed, and the two defects that made an operator-stated charter impossible to honour are fixed at head 9f30db4245ea2831297de51840343e9e3699b690 — awaiting codex's review, so please do not act on this before that lands.\n\nWhy this needs you specifically. A charter is policy, and the connector requires it to be stated and ratified by an actor holding operator standing. Claude and codex are not operators, and I will not sign as you. This is the one step in the whole flow that no agent can take.\n\nThe exact shape, so this is one action rather than a negotiation. A propose carrying body fields connector=github, owner=generalbusiness-ai, repo=gitseq, actor=github-connector, and operations=\"observe propose\" — then ratify it. The operations field is what makes it an outbound charter: a charter that declares no operations authorizes observation only, deliberately, so that a charter written for reading can never quietly acquire the power to write to the forge.\n\nTwo things worth knowing before you state it.\n\nIt will be stale the moment you write it, if it replaces the current charter, because a replacement must cite what it replaces and what it replaces is then retired. That is now fine and was not before; the connector reports the staleness rather than refusing the charter. This is exactly the defect you predicted when you told me to file the underlying issue.\n\nOpening a pull request on a public repository cannot be taken back by any act in this workroom. The charter is what authorizes that, so it is worth reading the scope rather than accepting mine: what I have described bounds it to one connector, one owner, one repository, one actor, and two named operations, and the admission clauses bound which issues are read on top of that.\n\nIf you would rather scope it more narrowly — observation only for now, or a different actor — say so and the dogfood waits. I would rather it wait than have you ratify a doorstep you have not chosen.","body":{"conditions":"A propose stating a charter whose body carries connector=github, owner=generalbusiness-ai, repo=gitseq, actor=github-connector and operations naming both observe and propose, or a deliberately narrower scope of hugh's choosing; that propose ratified by an actor holding operator standing; stated after codex's verdict on head 9f30db4245ea2831297de51840343e9e3699b690 lands, so the charter is not written against a head that may still change","to":"7fbc80f1ba06266cc375cb00507b94a631e5bed989180ad849fcd63175938275"}}